knext bundled fix for vinext 1.0.1 (dist output)
Upstream: https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/pull/3734
What it fixes: `/_next/image` responses now carry `x-nextjs-cache: MISS` like Next.js does (vinext has no image cache, so every successful response is a fresh optimization); error responses and a 304 carry no header.
Next.js sends it on every successful image response and its own og-api e2e asserts
`x-nextjs-cache: MISS` on the first optimized request. This is the maintainer's header-only
version of the upstream PR: the header is set with the other success headers in
image-optimization.js (transformed, passthrough and SVG-passthrough), and the Node production
server sends it only with the image bytes (200/206) it serves from its static cache.
Retire: delete this file (and its manifest entry) when the pinned vinext is >= the first
release that includes cloudflare/vinext#3734.
Ported by hand from the upstream src change to the published 1.0.1 dist files.
Applied by `knext vinext-patches` (runs from the app's postinstall and before `knext build`).

